course: dictionary
lesson: 6029
title: One spelling, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words come from other languages, and they can look like ordinary English words. The spelling mei is not an English word. In Mandarin Chinese, written in pinyin with tone marks, méi means «not» and měi means «beautiful» or «every». The mark over the letter changes the meaning.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. «Every Sunday Mei-Lin in London video calls her cousin in Shanghai.» The capital M shows that Mei-Lin is a name, and Shanghai is a city, so this sentence is about people and places, not a word from Mandarin.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «měitiān», the měi means every, so měitiān means every day. Does «every day» fit the sense of the sentence? If it does, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Mei is a girl's name used in China and Japan, and to an English ear it sounds like «may».
fact: «Méi» means «not» or «don't have»; «méiyǒu» means «there isn't» or «I haven't got».
fact: «Měi» means «beautiful» and also «every»; «měitiān» means «every day».
fact: «Měiguó» means «America», the USA, and literally means «beautiful country».
fact: In pinyin, tone marks change the meaning, so méi and měi are spelled almost the same but mean different things.
exercise: In Mandarin, «měitiān» means every day. Which English word matches měi in that word? | not | *every | America | beautiful
exercise: What does «méiyǒu» mean in Mandarin? | *there isn't, or I haven't got | a girl's name | beautiful country | every day
exercise: Mei is a girl's name. To an English ear, which word does it sound like? | like my | like mine | *like may | like me
test: Which Mandarin word means «not» or «don't have»? | *méi | měi | Měiguó | Mei
test: «Měiguó» is the Mandarin word for which country? | Japan | China | *America | Italy
exam: A Chinese friend says «méi guānxi». What does it mean? | It is every day | It is beautiful | *It doesn't matter, no problem | It is America
